### Assessment Summary

| Component | Criteria | Marks |
|-----------|----------|-------|
| **Written Critique** | Summary | 1 |
|  | Understanding | 2 |
|  | Strengths & Weaknesses | 3 |
|  | Scientific Reception | 2 |
|  | Impact | 2 |
|  | *Honours/Masters only: Citation Analysis* | 5 |
| **Oral Critique** | Understanding | 2 |
|  | Strengths & Weaknesses | 2 |
|  | Scientific Reception | 2 |
|  | Impact | 1 |
|  | Delivery | 1.5 |
|  | Slides | 1.5 |

---

By the end of this assessment, you should be able to:
- Critically evaluate scientific writing,
- Communicate complex ideas clearly,
- Understand how individual studies fit into broader research,
- Reflect on the role and influence of research within the scientific community,
- Provide fair, constructive feedback on the work of your peers.